  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Depth in zones – 2v1 and 2v3",
  "description": "The area, about 20 × 20 metres (not to scale), is split into a build-up zone and an attacking zone – roughly 40/60 to 50/50. The build-up zone has a bigger goal with a goalkeeper; the attacking zone has two small goals or two cones.\n\nThe attacking team has two players in each zone. The defending team has one player in the build-up zone and three in the attacking zone. That makes a 2v1 in the build-up and a 2v3 further forward. The attackers build up in their zone, pass in to a team-mate in the attacking zone and try to score in one of the small goals. The defenders try to stop the build-up and counter on the goal with the goalkeeper. After a turnover both teams may attack and defend in both zones.\n\nVariations: add jokers who play with the attacking team, or remove the zones and play freely. The big goal at the top end is not used.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Give the ball carrier options forward, backward and diagonally – do not stand in a line."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Run in depth when the ball carrier has time and can see you."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Position yourself so you can receive and take the ball straight towards goal."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Use the extra player in the build-up: draw the defender before you pass."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
